import SwiftUI

struct TableOutputInformationView:View {
    var body:some View {
        VStack(alignment:.leading,spacing:9) {
            Text("Save the complete connected table to an explicitly granted local folder or database destination. An empty included-column list means all columns in incoming order. Search filters the grid only. Apply saves one undoable draft; Revert restores saved settings.")
            Text("Stop protects existing files. Replace atomically creates a whole new file or workbook and verifies the destination has not changed. Excel never appends to existing sheets. History displays captured receipts and tables without writing again; a successful preparation write can remain if later training fails.")
            Text("CSV/TSV preserve numbers by default. Custom number/date patterns and apostrophe prefixes deliberately change the exported representation. Null text may coincide with a real empty/text value. CSV quoting does not prevent spreadsheet formula interpretation; choose the spreadsheet-text policy explicitly. Delimiters are one character. Supported encodings are UTF-8 and explicit UTF-16 byte orders.")
            Text("JSON records support null or omitted keys. Rows plus schema preserves ordered columns and positional nulls. NDJSON writes one compact record per line. Nonfinite numbers stop or become null. Integer temporal representation uses days for Date and microseconds for DateTime/Time; records require that unit knowledge, while rows plus schema includes typed metadata. ISO retains microseconds and explicit DateTime offsets.")
            Text("Parquet retains typed columns, temporal units and timezone metadata. Gzip levels 0–9, Brotli 0–11 and Zstandard −7–22 are supported; other codecs have no level control. Row groups bound row batches; data-page size is a target. Statistics is an actual writer option.")
            Text("Excel writes formula-like values as literal text. Values beyond exact Excel representation use Stop or Text: large integers, floats losing precision, timezone-bearing DateTime, dates before March 1900, and Time with submillisecond precision. Exact Date and millisecond Time use the selected date format. Start cell/header count toward Excel limits. One million written cells is the workbook memory allowance; choose Parquet for larger data.")
            Text("Images default to Stop. Copied assets creates a new atomic bundle directory containing the table, captured .kwipimg pixel bytes and a SHA-256 manifest. Table references are relative to that bundle; private source paths are never exported. Existing bundles cannot be replaced. Output files and whole image bundles have a 50 MB allowance. Cancellation before publication cleans staging; late cancellation cannot rewrite an accepted historical receipt.")
            Text("API sends JSON requests for the complete prepared table. Apply saves settings; only Run Flow sends requests. Use individual rows or batches, map source columns to JSON Pointer destinations and choose explicit value types. Null cells become JSON null. A private profile authorizes requests to exactly one origin and authentication mode. Authentication values remain in Keychain, outside portable graphs and History.")
            Text("API writes run sequentially at the configured rate. No automatic write retries occur. An endpoint-supported idempotency header receives a stable operation/request key; a new Run Flow is a new operation. HTTP acceptance does not prove downstream completion or individual batch-record processing. A failed response can leave earlier requests accepted; a lost response leaves an uncertain outcome. Check delivery and acknowledge before a new write. Receipt viewing never sends requests. Optional response extraction is bounded and may contain endpoint data; omit it when not needed. Component-output capture off prevents collecting/storing optional response bodies; delivery metadata and the verified input remain required evidence. Output field paths create nested objects; use JSON columns or constants for arrays.")
            Text("Database supports SQLite, PostgreSQL and MySQL. Test connection reads metadata only; Apply saves configuration; Run Flow performs the write. Choose an existing SQLite file and grant its containing folder for journals. Remote credentials live in private connection profiles shared with Table Input. Enable Table Output writes for a profile explicitly. TLS verifies certificates/hostnames; unencrypted access is limited to literal loopback addresses.")
            Text("Create never replaces a table. Append uses known writable columns and server defaults for omitted columns. Upsert uses every member of an existing unique key; incoming keys must be nonmissing and unique. Existing database types are read-only. Use Columns to convert incompatible values. Image/token-sequence, binary and arbitrary-precision columns need an explicit supported scalar representation first.")
            Text("Each destination has one row transaction across its batches. MySQL requires InnoDB; its table creation is a separate schema change, and its Upsert requires exactly one unique key. A committed receipt confirms transaction acknowledgment, not separate inserted/updated counts. On an unknown outcome, inspect the database and explicitly acknowledge the receipt before a new write. Writes already committed remain if another destination or later training fails. History never repeats a write.")
            Text("Database dispatch uses the app’s isolated network service after verifying the complete prepared table. The input capture is bounded to 50 MB and five million cells; shared run/storage budgets still apply. Portable preparation Code deliberately refuses database writes without the native credential/permission broker; it does not embed credentials or pretend a write succeeded.")
            Text("Folder grants stay local and outside portable graphs. Portable Code replay asks for new explicit destination bindings and uses the pinned writer dependencies. File destinations support CSV/TSV, Parquet, JSON/NDJSON and Excel.")
        }.font(.caption).foregroundStyle(MLTheme.muted).textSelection(.enabled)
    }
}
